    {"id": 4, "claim": "Salmonid eggs and early life stages are osmotically intolerant of saline water and require low-salinity, oxygen-rich freshwater gravel beds for successful development.", "evidence": "Physiological studies on salmonid reproduction show that eggs cannot survive or hatch in the saline conditions of the Caspian Sea.", "weight": 0.35, "depends_on": [2]},
